    <description>Fires exactly once per Consider-to-Explore transition (prior stage was literally Consider, current stage is Explore - not just &quot;entered Explore from anywhere&quot;), so it does not re-fire on later saves while already in Explore. Auto-creates one AF_TestDrive__c and one Appraisal (PurposeType=Trade-In) linked to the Opportunity, both seeded from the Opportunity&apos;s Account/Brand/Primary Contact. UPDATED 2026-09-14: each creation is now independently gated on whether the Opportunity already has ANY linked AF_TestDrive__c / Appraisal (Get_Existing_TestDrive, Get_Existing_Appraisal - any status, not just open ones) - if one already exists, this flow skips creating another for that side, so an Opportunity that cycles back to Consider and forward to Explore again no longer accumulates a fresh duplicate pair every time. The two sides are checked and created independently, so if only one of the two (say the Appraisal) already exists, the missing one (Test Drive) still gets created. Also carries forward the Lead-side test-drive interest (Lead Convert already maps AF_TestDriveDateTime__c/AF_TestDriveLocation__c onto the Opportunity&apos;s AF_CarriedTestDrive* fields) so a customer&apos;s pre-stated preference isn&apos;t lost — if a date/time was captured, the new Test Drive starts as Scheduled instead of Requested. UPDATED 2026-09-15: when a new Trade-In Appraisal is actually created (chained off Create_Appraisal, so it never fires again for an Opportunity that already has one from a prior Explore cycle), also creates a Task for the Opportunity Owner prompting them to raise the trade-in option with the customer, and — if the Primary Brand Contact has an email on file — sends that customer an email explaining how trade-in works.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>TestDriveInitialStatus</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    OR(
        ISBLANK({!$Record.AF_CarriedTestDriveDateTime__c}),
        ISBLANK({!$Record.AF_CarriedTestDriveLocation__c})
    ),
    &quot;Requested&quot;,
    &quot;Scheduled&quot;
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>TradeInEmailSubject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;You Could Trade In Your Current Car – &quot; &amp; {!$Record.Name}</expression>
    </formulas>
